---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const UPDATED = "November 4, 2026";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Study Timer Online handles your data: what stays in your browser, which cookies and third-party services (Google Analytics, Google AdSense) are used, and your choices." canonicalPath="/privacy">
  <section class="page-band" style="padding-block: 3rem 6rem;">
    <div class="container-page" style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <article class="card legal-copy" style="padding: clamp(28px, 6vw, 56px); border-radius: 28px; line-height: 1.8;">
        <header style="margin-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--brand-a15); padding-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); font-weight: 800; color: var(--content-heading); margin: 0; line-height: 1.2;">Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0;">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>
        </header>

        <p>This policy explains what information Study Timer Online ("we", "the site") collects when you use studytimeronline.com, how it's used, and the choices you have. The site has no user accounts, and we don't ask for your name to use any tool.</p>

        <h2>1. Data stored on your device</h2>
        <p>Your timer settings, theme choice, planner tasks, completed sessions and streaks are saved in your browser's <strong>local storage</strong>, on your own device. This data isn't sent to our servers, and we can't see it. You can delete it at any time by clearing this site's data in your browser settings. Doing so permanently resets your stats and planner.</p>
        <p>Some timer settings can be put in the page address (for example, a custom duration) so that you can bookmark or share a link. Anyone you share that link with can see those settings.</p>

        <h2>2. Analytics</h2>
        <p>We use <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to understand how the site is used in aggregate: which pages are visited, roughly where visitors come from, what device and browser they use, and how long they stay. Google Analytics uses cookies and similar technologies, and processes your IP address to do this. We use the reports to decide what to improve. We don't use them to identify individual visitors.</p>
        <p>You can opt out of Google Analytics on all websites by installing the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p>

        <h2>3. Advertising</h2>
        <p>We use, or may use, <strong>Google AdSense</strong> to show ads, which help keep the site free. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your previous visits to this and other websites.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Google's use of advertising cookies lets it and its partners serve ads to you based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the internet.</li>
          <li>You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting Google's <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalised advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info</a>.</li>
          <li>To learn more, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you're in the European Economic Area, the UK or Switzerland, you'll be asked for consent before personalised ads or non-essential cookies are used, and you can change your choice at any time.</p>

        <h2>4. Contact form</h2>
        <p>If you use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>, the email address, country and message you enter are sent through <strong>FormSubmit</strong> (formsubmit.co), which forwards them to our inbox. We use them only to reply to you, and we don't add you to any mailing list.</p>

        <h2>5. Hosting and server logs</h2>
        <p>The site is hosted on <strong>Cloudflare</strong>. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical information such as IP addresses and request details to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse.</p>

        <h2>6. Notifications, sound and voice</h2>
        <p>Alarms, voice cues and desktop notifications run entirely in your browser. Notifications are only shown if you grant permission when your browser asks, and you can revoke it at any time in your browser settings.</p>

        <h2>7. Children</h2>
        <p>The site is a general-audience study tool and isn't directed at children under 13. We don't knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>

        <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct or delete personal data held about you, or to object to its processing. Data in local storage is fully under your control. For anything else, such as a message you sent us, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> and we'll respond.</p>

        <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If we change this policy, we'll update the date at the top of this page.</p>

        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about privacy? Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
